    "Labels come from an off-board diagram with name columns on both sides of each dot column; the name next to the dot (e.g. 'MICN', 'TX1', 'CVB') and the far-side names were all kept, with GPIO names (IOxx) used as labels where printed.",
    "Left row 5 shows 'CVB' next to the pin and 'CVBS' further out; 'CVBS' used as label with 'CVB' as alternate spelling. Right rows 15-16 share one '5V in' / 'IN/OUT' box spanning both pins.",
    "Right row 11 shows 'IOG11' on both sides; right row 12 shows 'IRRX' near the pin and 'IOL11' further out."
